    <!-- Beast packages. These two troops each put MORE THAN ONE agent on the field, so their weight prices the whole
       package, not the rider: the rule is that every extra battlefield agent adds 1.0, which is what that archer
       would have cost as a troop of its own.

       War Elephant: 10.0 was set (c9fae4dc) while the howdah crew were parked, so it priced the beast and its mahout
       only. Crew came back on 2026-09-20 (#627) at two archers, so the package is 12.0.

       Mumakil: it had NO row until 2026-09-20, which meant the largest unit in the mod cost one party slot, the same
       as a peasant. Its monster is the elephant's on paper (500 hit points, weight 9999) but it is 3.0x the body with
       a 12 m trample radius against the elephant's 4 m, so beast and rider are worth about twice the elephant's, and
       the rule above would add eight for the platform crew: 28.0.

       It ships at 20.0, NOT 28.0, because 20 is the ceiling the weight system's identity was proven for
       (WeightedFrameIdentityTests.HeaviestShippedWeight_StaysWithinTheRangeTheIdentityWasProvenFor). Above it a
       normal party-size limit can fall under a single troop's weight, which makes the clamped single-body boundary
       reachable and lets the displayed over-capacity verdict disagree with the enforced one. So the mumakil is
       deliberately under-priced by about eight, and raising it means re-deriving that identity first. -->
    <TroopWeight id="harad_elephant_rider" weight="12.0" />
    <TroopWeight id="harad_mumakil_rider" weight="20.0" />

